  "articleBody": "Thinking about a new shower? It's a great way to refresh your bathroom, but sometimes it’s definitely a job for the pros. If you're looking to move any plumbing lines, like rerouting water supply or changing the drain's location, that's a big indicator. Even small changes can affect water pressure and drainage if not done right. Also, if your bathroom involves intricate waterproofing or structural adjustments, especially with custom tile or glass enclosures, you'll want an expert on board. They ensure everything is sealed correctly to prevent leaks and that the structure can handle the new weight. Don't forget about local building codes and permits, which can be tricky to navigate. A qualified installer, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, knows these regulations and ensures your project complies, saving you headaches down the road. If your project touches on any of these points, give us a call at 303-505-0866; we can make sure your new shower is installed perfectly and safely.",
